  (text "BoltATAS - design notes" (at 162.56 165.10 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.7 1.7)) (justify left top)) (uuid 9d2dc81f-1616-59d3-be1d-899d8af7481b))
  (text "Tandem match (Sontheimer): T1 = current transformer, 30T from GND to FWD_PORT; T2 = voltage transformer,\n30T from RF_LINE to GND, its 1T (coax centre) between FWD_PORT and REF_PORT. Both coax braids grounded at ONE end.\nFWD and REF swapped when testing? Swap the two 30T leads of T1.\nCoupling 20log(30) = 29.5 dB + 13 dB pi-pad = 42.5 dB: 120 W -> +8.3 dBm at the AD8307 (linear to +16 dBm),\n200 W -> 2.36 V at the ADC (ESP32 linear to 2.45 V). Pad = 50 ohm port load: 78.7 || (105 + 31.6||1.1k) = 49.8 ohm.\nDC is injected AFTER the DC block C1..C3: it must never reach T2 (its 30T winding is a DC short) or the radio.\nMotor: K1 NC feeds K2 COM, so 12 V and 8 V can never meet; K1 wins. Idle: motor line to 0 V via R41.\nAD8307: OUT unloaded (25 mV/dB, 12.5k internal), ENB tied to VPS, INM AC-coupled, 1 uF on OFS for 160 m.\nL1: 20 turns 0.8 mm CuL on FT114-43 (about 240 uH); measure |Z| >= 1.5 kohm over 1.8-30 MHz with a VNA.\nRelays: pin numbers per the KiCad SRD footprint (1 COM, 3 NO, 4 NC); check COM-NC continuity before soldering.\nWT32-ETH01: IO0 is the 50 MHz Ethernet clock input, keep R50 right at the socket. Front panel: see block F.\nTune only with <= 25 W carrier (firmware refuses above). Heatsinks on U1 and U2 (motor current).\nFront panel (F): buttons 10k pull-up + 100n = 1 ms debounce, 1k protects the GPIO. IO2/IO12 are strap pins:\nthe LED to GND keeps them low at boot. IO5/IO15 are strap pins too: a pull-up is their default level.\nJ5 = front panel option: buttons in parallel; fit the LEDs on the board OR on the panel (series R stays on the board)." (at 162.56 170.18 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid d120cc9b-3b53-502b-9c9a-d45407162a19))

